VIOLATION — MUST-3: every MUST or MUST NOT clause MUST include a concrete example showing BOTH
the correct and the blocked pattern. Clause 2 of this file shows only the correct one.

Clause 1 is complete: its block carries a `# DO` arm with both bounds declared and a `# DO NOT`
arm showing the attempt-ceiling-only call with the backoff arithmetic that makes it wrong.
Clause 2's block carries a `# DO` arm alone — the keyed re-send — and stops. The pattern the
clause BLOCKS, an unkeyed re-send of an undetermined write, is described in prose in the
clause body and is never SHOWN. The unambiguous anchor MUST-3 exists to supply is therefore
absent for that clause, and an agent reading the block by itself learns what to do and not
what it is being stopped from doing.

The defect is a missing ARM, not a missing block. The fence is present, the language is
right, the example compiles; one half of the required contrast is simply not there.

Discriminator 1 — MUST-1 IS SATISFIED. Every load-bearing sentence in both clauses uses MUST
or MUST NOT and names the alternative BLOCKED. No "should," "prefer," "consider" or "try to"
appears as a clause modal anywhere in the file.

Discriminator 2 — MUST-2 IS SATISFIED. The `**BLOCKED rationalizations:**` corpus holds six
literal first-person sentences a session would really emit ("A timeout almost always means the
request never landed"), not abstract category labels. A judge citing MUST-2 has named a defect
this file does not contain.

Discriminator 3 — MUST-4 IS SATISFIED, and this is the closest neighbour. Clause 2 DOES carry
its `**Why:**` line, one sentence, naming the failure mode. The clause is not unexplained; it
is unexemplified. A judge that reads the truncated block and reaches for the missing-Why
clause has named the wrong one.

Discriminator 4 — MUST-5, MUST-6 and MUST-7 ARE SATISFIED. Frontmatter declares `priority: 10`
with `scope: path-scoped` and a matching `paths:` list; Origin cites
`journal/0431-INCIDENT-duplicate-order-storm.md` § 1 with the measured duplicate count.

Discriminator 5 — MUST-8 IS NOT ENGAGED (no CLI-divergent content), MUST-9 IS NOT ENGAGED (no
empirical-validation fixtures ship), and MUST-10 / MUST-11 ARE NOT ENGAGED (`priority: 10` +
`scope: path-scoped`, excluded by Rule 10's own Trigger-scope paragraph).

Discriminator 6 — THE `## MUST NOT` BULLETS ARE SATISFIED. Every `**Why:**` is one sentence; no
hedging phrase sits inside a MUST clause; the Detection row names AST call nodes, keyword
presence and header-dict membership, all parsed structure; the file is well under 200 lines.

The whole defect is the `# DO NOT` arm that clause 2 never shows.
